  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the Yoda figurine as the speaker of the misogynistic message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the Yoda_figurine, which is visually and textually presented as the entity uttering the offensive line 'beat women i must'. This projection is established through the analogical mapping where the visual material (Yoda_figurine) is directly associated with the textual material (top_text and bottom_text) to create the scene. The user, as the viewer, is implicitly positioned as the one who understands the parody and the character's role in delivering the message, even though no explicit deictic pronoun like 'me' or 'you' appears in the text. The projection is onto the visual material (Yoda_figurine) as the agent performing the action described in the text.",
